cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite the associated paper."
title: "RepSpace: Representation Space Decides - A Platform-Independent Measurement and Generalization-Diagnosis Framework for Interaction-Data Structure Prediction"
abstract: >-
  An anonymized reproducibility artifact for a data-centric evaluation paper.
  It contains the full pipeline (corpus construction, representation-space
  profiling, calibrated probes, cross-tier transfer experiments, chain-level
  metrics, and an LLM event-chain backtracking mechanism), all result files
  needed to rebuild every table and figure, and a verification script that
  reproduces the published numbers without requiring the original corpora.
type: software
license: MIT
version: "1.0"
keywords:
  - conversation disentanglement
  - benchmark evaluation
  - representation space
  - weak supervision
  - dataset bias
  - chain-level metrics
